<title>USA: U.S. Dec business inventories fell 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Dec business inventories fell 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. December business inventories fell 0.1 percent after remaining unchanged in November. It said December business sales also fell 0.1 percent after a revised 0.4 percent increase in November.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>INVENTORIES:    December  November---Rev from  October</p>
<p> Total Business  1,009.46  1,010.92  1,011.96  1,011.26</p>
<p> Durable Goods     607.43    608.93    609.44    610.32</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  402.04    401.98    402.52    400.94</p>
<p> Manufacturers     438.17   439.37    439.89     438.13</p>
<p> Retailers	   314.96   313.62    314.05     315.36</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     88.76    87.93     87.86</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 256.34   257.93    258.02     257.77</p>
<p>    SALES:	 December  November---Rev from  October</p>
<p> Total Business    727.76   728.80    729.83     725.79</p>
<p> Durable Goods     357.64   359.30    360.75     357.53</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  370.12   369.51    369.08     368.26</p>
<p> Manufacturers     315.56   317.55    318.28     315.51</p>
<p> Retailers	   207.87   207.32    206.97     207.49</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     51.10    50.58     50.55</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 204.34   203.93    204.58     202.79</p>
<p> Inventory-To-   December  November---Rev from  October</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.39     1.39	1.39	 1.39</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected December business inventories to fall 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised November inventories from a previously reported 0.1 percent increase and business sales from a 0.6 percent increase.</p>
